  "api_error_status": null,
  "result": "The node didn't pass. The only gate run (1 of 6) returned **`UNANCHORED_VARIABLE`**, and I stopped there because the node itself needs fixing. I wrote it up in `task_result.md`.\n\n**The problem:** the rule has to say the subject plans a right turn at an intersection or a driveway/alley entrance. That region isn't tied to the subject or to the turn lane by anything except the declared intention, and the gate doesn't accept an intention as a tie. Without one, the rule would accept a planned right turn at any intersection or driveway anywhere in the scene. The only tying atom the node claims is `rel.occupies`. Using it would mean \"the subject is in the intersection or driveway\", which is false while the vehicle is still in the turn lane, so it would change the duty.\n\n**Fix for the plan agent (span s3):** claim an atom that links the turn lane to the target region:\n- **Intersection:** `st.lane_enters` (the intersection the lane leads into). The forbid scenario already describes \"the intersection the lane enters\".\n- **Driveway or alley entrance:** something like `st.lane_connectivity`, or a geometry-distance atom with its own reach parameter. The plan agent should pick whichever the reading supports.\n\n**What's in the files:**\n- **Rule:** applies when the subject, a vehicle, occupies a turn lane on the right side. For every such lane, it requires a declared right turn at some intersection or some driveway/alley entrance. No narrowings are declared.\n- **Witnesses:** the four planned scenes (forbid, permit, idle, blind), plus two of my own: `branch_1` (left turn lane, expected not applicable) and `branch_2` (turn declared at the driveway only, expected compliant). None of them has been checked, because the gate stopped before running witnesses.\n\nOne of my shell commands (reading Core source files) was refused automatically because it set a variable. I read the same files with the file reader instead.",
